==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{recons|huzdą|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{recons|kusdʰo-||something hidden, hiding-place|lang=ine-pro}}, from {{recons|kew-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|kewə-||to cover, encase|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with Old Saxon {{term|hord||treasure, hiding-place|lang=osx}}, Old High German {{term|hort|lang=goh}} (German {{term|Hort||hoard, protection, refuge|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|hodd|lang=non}} (Swedish {{term|hudda||shelter|lang=sv}}), Gothic {{term|𐌷𐌿𐌶𐌳||tr=huzd|hidden hoard|lang=got}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/hoːrd/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|g=n|pl=hord}}

